            "The latest stable Electron release is **44.7.0**, from October 7, 2026. That's the newest entry on the official releases page, and it's the top of the 44.x line, the newest stable major.\n\n- 44.7.0 was released Oct 7, 2026, with Chromium 152.0.7977.130 and Node.js 24.21.0.\n- Electron 44 is the newest major version. It was announced August 25, 2026, with Chromium 152, V8 15.2 and Node v24.18.1.\n- Older supported lines are still getting patches. 43.7.9 and 42.11.12 were released Oct 6 and Oct 7.\n- Electron 45 isn't stable yet. Its alpha builds are on branch 45-x-y.\n\nSome other sources I found are out of date. The npm page showed 44.4.5 and Wikipedia showed 44.4.5, both older snapshots. The official releases site is the most current.\n\nTo install it, run `npm install electron@latest`."
